From b390c2a1183ba178bd8e0278af299d8ea0d91a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:06:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: omci: report an OLT profile change only when the
 effective profile changes

Setting the OLT profile reports a configuration change whenever the
configured value differs, and the xPON MAC restarts the GPON session for
it. With "auto", the agent already detects the profile from the OLT-G
right after O5, so when userspace later applies a configuration that
names the same profile ("auto" -> "huawei" with a Huawei OLT), nothing
the session depends on changes, but the ONU still drops out of O5 and
registers again.

Seen on the Archer XR500v on every boot with olt_profile 'huawei' in
UCI:

  OMCI OLT profile applied: configured=auto effective=huawei ...
  OMCI OLT profile applied: configured=huawei effective=huawei ...
  GPON session configuration changed (OMCI key 12), scheduling full restart

and O5 a second time about 6 s later.

omci_agent_profile_refresh_locked() already knows whether the effective
profile or its quirks changed. Use that for the profile keys, and keep
reporting the change when they do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 585edcecc..c992e4c8b 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -4595,6 +4595,7 @@ __omci_agent_config_set_source(struct omci_device *odev, u16 key,
 	u8 old_force;
 	u8 scalar;
 	bool profile_key = false;
+	bool profile_changed = false;
 	bool operational_changed = false;
 	bool changed = false;
 	int ret = 0;
@@ -4805,12 +4806,21 @@ __omci_agent_config_set_source(struct omci_device *odev, u16 key,
 	}
 	if (!ret && profile_key) {
 		olt = omci_agent_olt_g_locked(agent);
-		ret = omci_agent_profile_refresh_locked(odev, olt, NULL);
+		ret = omci_agent_profile_refresh_locked(odev, olt,
+							&profile_changed);
 		if (ret) {
 			agent->config.olt_profile = old_profile;
 			agent->config.olt_profile_force = old_force;
 			agent->config.olt_profile_source = old_profile_source;
 			agent->config.olt_profile_force_source = old_force_source;
+		} else if (!profile_changed) {
+			/*
+			 * Only the configured value changed, for example "auto"
+			 * to the profile "auto" had already detected. The
+			 * effective profile and its quirks are the same, so do
+			 * not report a change that would restart the session.
+			 */
+			changed = false;
 		}
 	}
 	if (!ret && changed && !profile_key) {
-- 
